# probe (quest rework P5): a zone-in event left open (rezone open) reaches its onEventUpdate, which the zone-in's own
# answers (a 0x05B finish) never could. I Can Hear a Rainbow (windurst 75; recorded on its Lua, which group 5 deleted: it now replays against ICanHearARainbow.cs) at Prog 0 in West Ronfaure with
# Carbuncle's Ruby: its zone-in plays 51 when the zone's weather is one whose element the Light var lacks. The login's
# zone-in plays 51 for the seeded weather and answers it at once (Light 1). Rain (6) set by GM, rezone open: 51 open (the
# Weather local var 6); its update: updateEvent(0, 1, 6, 1 light); its finish: Light 65 (the water bit). Thunder (14),
# rezone open: 51; update: updateEvent(0, 1, 14, 2 lights); finish: Light 97 (the thunder bit).
# Not a quest port: the key names no quest (Program.IsProbe).
char zone=WestRonfaure pos=-258.5,-71,423.4 job=SMN lvl=30
quest Windurst.ICanHearARainbow accepted
item CarbunclesRuby
login                       # 51 for the seeded weather, answered: Light 1
weather 6                   # RAIN
rezone open                 # 51 open
update 51 option=0          # updateEvent(0, 1, 6, 1)
finish                      # Light 65: the water bit
weather 14                  # THUNDER
rezone open                 # 51 open
update 51 option=0          # updateEvent(0, 1, 14, 2)
finish                      # Light 97: the thunder bit
